# Mathematical Working Drafts

Before choosing a fixed destination or retiring a draft, apply the [common content decision](../../framework/rules/records.md#substantive-material-retention) to its actual mathematics, existing homes and consumers.
Preserve useful failures and continuing work; setup-only residue needs no new material.
Follow the [kind-specific rules](../../framework/rules/ledger.md#working-drafts-and-fixed-findings).

Develop arguments, partial calculations, counterexample searches and continuing failure investigations directly here.
Link continued/reusable programs and native data through their responsible [J group](../../framework/rules/computations.md#computation-output-location), with generated output in `mathematics/computation/outputs/<J>/`.
This is durable research material, not an assertion of acceptance.
Fix a valuable failed finding in ledger as soon as it is useful for continuation or changes a research decision;
an unfinished Task is not a reason to retain that finding only in a mutable draft.
Small interactive trials need no new record.
Root `.tmp/` is reserved for [disposable operational isolation](../../framework/rules/organization.md#temporary-storage), with no mathematical scratch-directory stage.

## Naming and editing

Use `Author_D_W0001.md` for local mathematical drafts, with the author's chosen line and an independent D counter.
Public source drafts may be cited at an exact source revision; D is not an acquired material kind.
Develop new work in the responsible local draft.
Keep a descriptive title and the minimal author/source header from the [material format](../../framework/material-format.md); link the actual Task or Claim when relevant rather than copying its serial.
These are format examples, not existing drafts.
Retained computation programs and native data use their [J group](../../framework/rules/computations.md), linked from the draft.

Edit a working draft in place under its D address, stable during that use and reusable after retirement.
Do not add `_vN` for each iteration, maintain a draft registry, or publish a C/T record merely because a draft changed.
A separate working review has its own reviewing human's D address and precise draft/scope link; it does not automatically become a fixed R verdict.
Retain the assumptions, useful derivations, unresolved gaps and necessary scripts/data that help the next researcher continue; no mandatory per-edit log or template is required.

Live exploratory links may identify these files as working material.
They are not fixed proof support or acceptance evidence.
Authoritative Task/Claim records, strategy decisions and execution records remain in their responsible locations.
Do not relocate an already published mathematical version here to rewrite it.

## Valuable failed explorations

Fix valuable failed attempts in a versioned entry or suitable module section in [ledger](../ledger/readme.md).
Retain the question, hypotheses and tested range, decisive failed step or unresolved test, evidence and necessary scripts/data, what remains possible, and a useful next or reopening condition.
A fixed account may record an inconclusive observation; it does not by itself certify a refutation.
Reuse an adequate existing fixed account rather than duplicate it.

Link the relevant strategy, exact Claim/proof version and other evidence, explaining which route was tested, which implication failed or which applicability limit was discovered.
Preserve fixed evidence and authorship.
Received originals remain unchanged: place adaptations and scoped feedback in local materials with the source formulation and actual supporting evidence.
These references imply neither source endorsement nor automatic proof dependencies.
Link complete calculations and audits at their existing homes without duplicating their narratives.

Keep genuinely continuing investigations in drafts after the bounded failed finding is fixed.
Failure of a sufficient strategy or one proof attempt does not refute the original target; state the precise remaining scope and avoid repeating the same failed approach without a relevant change.

## Fixing material and cleaning up

The main agent ensures necessary material organization at the end of each exploration round under the [round-closeout rule](../../framework/rules/workflow.md#exploration-round-closeout), including results delivered by subagents with a restricted write scope.

1. Identify necessary content and adequate existing homes before choosing a destination.
   If the mathematics is already fixed and only redundant setup remains, update consumers and remove that residue without a new material.
   Preserve any unique argument, useful failure, review limitation or needed native work at its responsible destination: [Claims](../claims/readme.md), [Task contracts](../tasks/readme.md), [exploration and research records](../ledger/readme.md), [reviews](../audits/reviews/readme.md), [computations](../computations/readme.md), [definitions](../definitions/readme.md).
   A Claim argument belongs in the same or another applicable fixed C and contains the actual reasoning.
   Independent project-mathematics review accounts belong to fixed R; manuscript-specific review stays with its manuscript; suitable exploration, comparisons, syntheses and self-review/unknown findings may remain in L.
   Follow the destination's identity/version rules; never overwrite an existing fixed version.
   Keep the author/repository prefix where applicable.
2. Update the affected links and required fixed-material registration, and verify the fixed result contains the selected mathematics and necessary scripts/data.
   An acceptance review binds the fixed material, not a continuing mutable draft.
   Ordinary feedback during drafting does not freeze each intermediate edit.
3. Move actual Markdown links, manuscript source maps, program inputs and substantive prose dependencies to the fixed content before removing the corresponding draft.
   The retired D address may then be reused without inheriting earlier content, scope, review or authority; never overwrite an in-use draft.
   If only part has been promoted, retain genuinely continuing work in a reduced draft and fix valuable failed findings in ledger before cleanup.
   Do not keep a redundant working copy solely as a receipt for the move.

This is a local research operation: no extra promotion approval, cleanup certificate, navigation refresh per edit or full-repository mathematical audit is required.
Further development may use a working draft while the fixed result remains intact.
Preserve actual publication, evidence and execution-authorization boundaries.

Routine return-link, path and format maintenance in another registered author's local writable S material needs no actor change, duplicate feedback, approval or warning log.
Substantive contributions use the responsible human's own numbered materials linked to the original under the [identity rule](../../framework/rules/identity.md).
Tool capability does not authorize a substantive cross-author rewrite or taking over another human's Task/E.
Received originals retain their separate provenance and feedback boundary.
